* ------------------------------------------------------------------
* Example Pin Definition File for QSymGen2
*
* Implements: Microchip PIC16F15213/PIC16F15214 devices
* Author:     Robert Dunn
* Revised:    2026.05.13
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
* ---------------------------------
*
* Pin Definitions:  DIR NAME ALTTEXT [* COMMENT]
*
* Where: DIR = Pin direction: I (input), O (output), B (bi-directional), or X (for spacing).
*        NAME = Pin name.  Don't use duplicate names -- QSymGen2 doesn't warn you if you do.
*        ALTTEXT = Additional text to include on symbol, e.g., alternate pin functions.
*        COMMENT = Optional comment.  (Space required before '*'.)
*
* ---------------------------------
*
* D = descriptive text for symbol and DLL block [optional but recommended]
*
D Microchip PIC16F15213/PIC16F15214
*
* Pin Definitions
*
I VDD
B RA0 ICSPDAT 
B RA1 ICSPCLK
I RA2 MCLR/VPP
X ---
X ---
B RA3 
B RA4 
B RA5 
I VSS
X ---
I CLK
*
*** EOF ***